// `andesim profile [--engine <id>] [report flags] ELF [-- <qemu args>]`.
//
// Hot inner-loop detection on the FUNCTIONAL engine, configured like the
// hybrid fast leg: profile picks a cycle-accurate engine (--engine or the
// sole one, the same selector cycle/hybrid use) and derives the QEMU launch
// from it -- the CPU model from the engine's `--print-qemu-config` driver
// globals, vlen from its --describe, and the staged qemu.cfg as -readconfig.
// That keeps the profiled ISA identical to the engine the reported
// `measure: --pc-start/--pc-end` windows will be measured on (a wrong vlen
// changes vsetvl trip counts, i.e. the hot-loop ranking itself).
//
// QEMU runs the ELF to completion with the hotIterationLoop TCG plugin; the
// plugin's
// `-d plugin -D` log is parsed, filtered (min-iters, RVV-only), nested, and
// rendered as the LLM Markdown report (or --no-llm table). All pure logic
// lives in profile.cpp; this file owns the IO: engine resolve, the cfg probe,
// the QEMU spawn, objdump/addr2line, and the per-loop symbol lookups.
